<title>UK: NatWest prices 300 mln stg structured bond.</title>
<headline>NatWest prices 300 mln stg structured bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond has been priced, lead manager NatWest Markets said on Tuesday.</p>
<p> BORROWER   NATIONAL WESTMINSTER BANK PLC</p>
<p> AMT    300 MLN STG   COUPON     8.125     MATURITY   *29.DEC.11</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  100.867   PAY DATE    19.DEC.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.00	REOFFER    99.267    SPREAD	+60 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	AA3	 LISTING    LONDON    PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AA-	 DENOMS (K) 10-100    SALE LIMITS US/UK</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    =	   HOME CTRY  BRITAIN   TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.40	SELL CONC  1.60	PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p> UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 7.50 PCT GILT DUE 2006</p>
<p> NOTES     *CALL AT PAR ON 29.DEC.06. IF NOT CALLED THE COUPON</p>
<p>		WILL BE RESET, IF NECESSARY, TO GIVE A 160 BP YIELD</p>
<p>		SPREAD OVER THE PREVAILING FIVE-YEAR GILT.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658  </p>
<p>		IBCA RATING IS AA.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
